From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:01:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: DOM Range, Element
 normalize/hasAttributes/scopeName/adjacent text/attributes (3015)

IHTMLDOMRange (document.createRange() in IE9 mode) returned E_NOTIMPL from all
but a couple of members. They are now wired to the Gecko range: startContainer,
startOffset, endContainer, endOffset, collapsed, commonAncestorContainer,
setStart, setEnd, setStartBefore/After, setEndBefore/After, collapse,
selectNode, selectNodeContents, compareBoundaryPoints, deleteContents,
extractContents, cloneContents, insertNode, surroundContents, cloneRange,
toString, detach, getClientRects and getBoundingClientRect.

IHTMLElement4::normalize and IHTMLElement6::hasAttributes use the Gecko node.
IHTMLElement2::scopeName reports the HTML namespace. getAdjacentText and
replaceAdjacentText work on the text node next to the element (beforeBegin,
afterBegin, beforeEnd, afterEnd); replaceAdjacentText creates the text node when
there is none. clearAttributes removes every attribute except id and name;
mergeAttributes (IHTMLElement2 and IHTMLElement3, whose flag controls whether id
and name are copied too) copies the attributes of another element.

